Add a cargo-fuzz target `ndjson` (upstream has none)

A lean4export NDJSON stream, loaded by the sequential reference loader
(parse::load) and checked declaration by declaration in file order on one
Checker, as one `palladium` worker does: the first rejection ends the
check; a fault (resource limit) replaces the checker and checking goes on;
the store is reset past RESET_TERMS terms, as in main.rs.
Upstream: none (no fuzz targets upstream, checked 2026-11-22).

